<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beneš decrees</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beneš decrees were the laws issued by the Czechoslovak president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edvard-benes">Edvard Beneš</a> in exile and in 1945 before the parliament reconvened. They provided for the confiscation of property of Germans, Hungarians and collaborators and the loss of their citizenship, forming the legal basis of the expulsion of some three million Germans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benes-decrees.jpg" alt="Beneš decrees" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown . Transfer; United States. Office of War Information. Overseas Picture Division. Washington Division; ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edvard_Bene%C5%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
